---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/* /canon — página dedicada de respaldo académico al libro Wenumapu
   (Canio & Pozo, OCHOLIBROS 2015) que da nombre a esta marca.
   Spec: ~/Obsidian/WenuAgent/brand/02-visual-system/spec-footer-cita-academica.md
*/

const voices = [
  'Clementina Neculfilu', 'Marta Parra', 'Aurelia Domihual', 'Seberiana Ancanao',
  'Juana Beltrán', 'Aurora Quidel', 'Margarita Canio', 'Victorina Canio',
  'Ángela Llanquinao', 'María Angélica Llanquinao', 'María Angélica Llancavil',
  'María Pulman', 'Laura Aillapan', 'Segundo Aninao', 'Juan Canio', 'Ramón Naupa',
  'Bernardo Mariluan', 'Víctor Ancan', 'Cristóbal Huincateo', 'Alejandro Huilcapan',
  'Belisario Pitriqueo', 'José Meliñir', 'Raúl Levi', 'Luis Llanquinao',
  'Domiciano Cabrera', 'Eugenio Millaqueo', 'Antonio Mariláf', 'Juan Segundo Huenufil',
  'Ramón Huenufil', 'Antonio Cayupul',
];

const bookLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Book',
  name: 'Wenumapu — Astronomía y Cosmología Mapuche',
  author: [
    { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Margarita Canio Llanquinao' },
    { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Gabriel Pozo Menares' },
  ],
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'OCHOLIBROS' },
  datePublished: '2015',
  isbn: '978-956-335-205-4',
  inLanguage: ['es', 'arn'],
  about: ['Astronomía Mapuche', 'Cosmología Mapuche', 'Wallmapu', 'Mapuzungun'],
  url: 'https://wenumapuonline.com/canon',
};
---

<Base
  title="Source · The book that named us — Wenu Mapu"
  description="Wenu Mapu honra la cosmovisión mapuche documentada por Margarita Canio Llanquinao y Gabriel Pozo Menares en Wenumapu (OCHOLIBROS, 2015 · ISBN 978-956-335-205-4)."
  jsonLd={bookLd}
>
  <article class="canon-page">
    <header class="canon__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">SOURCE</p>
      <h1 class="canon__title">The book that named us</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="canon__body">
      <p class="canon__lede">
        <strong>Wenu Mapu</strong> — the world above — is not a name invented
        by this brand. It is a cosmological concept of the Mapuche people,
        systematically documented by two Mapuche scholars who dedicated years
        to recording the astronomy and cosmology of their nation:
        <strong>Margarita Canio Llanquinao</strong> (Lof Kuzako, native
        mapuzungun speaker) and <strong>Gabriel Pozo Menares</strong> (PhD
        in History of the Americas).
      </p>

      <h2>About the book</h2>
      <p>
        <cite>Wenumapu — Astronomía y Cosmología Mapuche</cite> (OCHOLIBROS,
        Temuco, 2015) gathers the knowledge of dozens of mapuche speakers from
        the Wallmapu — the territories known today as Chile and Argentina. It
        is a bilingual text, in mapuzungun and Spanish, with celestial
        illustrations.
      </p>
      <p class="canon__isbn">ISBN 978-956-335-205-4</p>

      <h2>The 30 voices of the oral record</h2>
      <p>
        The book gathers the voices of 30 mapuche speakers who contributed
        accounts in their original language. Their names are printed in every
        copy of the book; we reproduce them here in recognition:
      </p>
      <ul class="canon__voices">
        {voices.map(v => <li>{v}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>Our position</h2>
      <p>
        This brand operates commercially as <strong>Wenu Mapu SpA</strong>.
        It is a ritual-jewelry project founded in Truckee, California by
        <strong>Nicolás Ortega García</strong>. It is <em>not</em> a
        Mapuche cultural institution, nor an officially authorised ethnic seal.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are <strong>readers</strong> of this book — not its authors. The
        knowledge it contains belongs to the Mapuche speakers who shared it,
        and to the scholars who transcribed and translated it. We work with
        this cosmovision because it has taught us, and we carry it on the
        body with care.
      </p>
      <p>
        We acknowledge the authors. We direct readers towards the book. We do
        not claim academic authority over the contents of the book itself.
      </p>

      <h2>To go deeper</h2>
      <p>
        The book is available in bookstores in Chile (Buscalibre, OCHOLIBROS
        direct) and by international order. We recommend reading it in full to
        truly understand what we are carrying on the body.
      </p>

      <p class="canon__cta">
        <a href="https://www.ocholibros.cl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          OCHOLIBROS →
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
